            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "lisa"
            },
            "reviewBody": "5 stars for flavor but 1 1/2 tsp of butter was def not enough. I ended up throwing in 2 Tbl more &amp; my shallots &amp; asparagus still wanted to stick &amp; burn. I think I'll add a bit of Evoo next time. Thanks, Kathi!!",
            "datePublished": "2012-06-03T15:32:03.317Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Where2gonexttime"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Since my oven was hot, I decided to roast the asparagus rather than fry/steam them. I tossed the shallots and asparagus with olive oil and seasoned them with salt and pepper. Roasted them at 425 for about 12 minutes, then added crumbled bacon (pre cooked) and cooked for 3-4 more minutes. Next time I might add a little fresh lemon juice. I think this would be good with green beans too.",
            "datePublished": "2022-05-05T02:16:20.271Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "PeppySoup8124"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great Recipe! I made it as written with the addition of a splash of acid (lemon juice) at the very end, right before serving. Also, I used a cast iron skillet to cook the bacon then again for \"Step 3\" frying the asparagus and shallots, that gave it a really nice char in the same 5 minute time allotted for step 3. Very yummy!",
            "datePublished": "2024-04-23T22:00:52.008Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
